            "review_title": "Review at Anh Tuyet Grilled Chicken",
            "review_text": "HCMCuisine\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam6 contributions\n0\nChicken Butt\nApr 2016 • Friends\nA small, dingy spot in Binh Thanh District, Ga Nuong Anh Tuyet has a reputation for serving up some fine chicken butt. The place is pretty standard: roadside barbecue, no air-con and a constant buzz of activity right outside. The staff are young, the chairs are tiny and the grill is practically on the street.\n\nFor me, it was a tie between the chicken butt (phao câu) and the grilled squid; both were excellent. Thanks to the barbecue, the former is crispy and firm on the outside and fatty and tender on the inside. No cartilage, no bones, just piping hot and delicious. The squid was also a hit: not too chewy, and with the green chili sauce, utterly delicious.\n\nAs for the duck tongues, I am still confused as to the anatomy of a duck because there was a bone attached. How does that work? Apart from logistics, there wasn't much meat to enjoy here, so I give it a pass.\n\nThe okra, however, was a worthy supplement to all of the greasy barbecue we consumed along with a few ice-cold beers. All told, Ga Nuong Anh Tuyet makes for a top-notch nhậu spot and well worth a visit. If you're especially squeamish, there are always wings available, but it's better to be open-minded; the phao câu might surprise you.\n\nIf you liked this review, be sure to read my other ones.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten April 8, 2016",
